Add a 64-bit ARM Linux host. config.gcc decodes the host as it does the
target, and stops at a machine it does not know, which aarch64 is, since
it came a decade later. Nothing it describes is used for the host, as for
x86_64, so the entry is empty.

--- a/gcc/config.gcc
+++ b/gcc/config.gcc
@@ -1329,6 +1329,8 @@
 	gnu_ld=yes
 	float_format=i386
 	;;
+aarch64-*-linux*)	# 64-bit ARM GNU/Linux, only ever as the host
+	;;
 i[34567]86-*-gnu*)
 	float_format=i386
 	;;
